caption: Boilerplate: realm scoping
tags: $:/tags/hypergsd/Docs
title: $:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/docs/api/boilerplates/realm-scoping

Copy-paste pattern for scoping ''your own'' lists to the realm selection made in the review sidebar. The plugin's canonical implementation is `modules/realm-scopes.tid` (`hgsd-realm-selection`, `hgsd-realm-all`, `hgsd-scope-include`/`-exclude`) — consumed by `$hgsd.pick`, `$hgsd.pick-field` and `$hgsd.list` through their `realm-scope` attribute (always evaluated; omitted = the selection, `""` = everything via `hgsd-realm-all`). The hand-rolled derivation below remains as the explanation of what the define does.

! The state contract

`$:/config/hypergsd/realm-selection` — one `list` field holding:

* the full realm tag titles that are ticked (`$:/GSD/Realm/Work`, …), and
* the literal sentinel `no-realm` when "Items not in a realm" is ticked.

Missing tiddler = pristine = all realms + sentinel (everything). An ''empty'' list = deliberately nothing (the sentinel may re-add the realm-less items). Distinguish with `!is[tiddler]`.

! The snippet

```
<$let base={{{ [tag[$:/GSD/MyType]format:titlelist[]join[ ]] }}}
    all-realms={{{ [all[tags]prefix[$:/GSD/Realm/]format:titlelist[]join[ ]] }}}
    selection={{{ [[$:/config/hypergsd/realm-selection]get[list]enlist-input[]!match[no-realm]format:titlelist[]join[ ]] }}}
    shown={{{ [title[$:/config/hypergsd/realm-selection]!is[tiddler]limit[1]] :then[enlist<all-realms>] [enlist<selection>] +[unique[]format:titlelist[]join[ ]] }}}
    show-realmless={{{ [title[$:/config/hypergsd/realm-selection]!is[tiddler]] [title[$:/config/hypergsd/realm-selection]get[list]enlist-input[]match[no-realm]] +[unique[]format:titlelist[]join[ ]] }}}>
<$list filter="[enlist<base>] -[all[tags]prefix[$:/GSD/Realm/]tagging[]] [enlist<shown>tagging[]] :filter[enlist<base>match<currentTiddler>]">
    …your rows…
</$list>
</$let>
```

(Drop the realm-less subtraction run when your list should honour "Items not in a realm" being unticked — wrap the two-leg formula in an `<%if [<show-realmless>!match[]] %>` branch, as `$hgsd.list` does.)

Deriving the two working values:

| !Value | !Filter | !Meaning |
|shown |`[title[state]!is[tiddler]limit[1]] :then[enlist<all-realms>] [enlist<selection>] +[unique[]…]` |the realms to show — `:then` supplies all realms only when the state tiddler is missing |
|show-realmless |`[title[state]!is[tiddler]] [title[state]get[list]enlist-input[]match[no-realm]] +[unique[]…]` |non-empty when the sentinel is present ''or'' pristine |

Scoping rule: ''items of any shown realm'' ∪ ''realm-less items when show-realmless'':

```
[your-base-filter] -[all[tags]prefix[$:/GSD/Realm/]tagging[]] [enlist<shown>tagging[]] :filter[your-base-constraint]
```

* `[enlist<shown>tagging[]]` — the tagging operator over multiple inputs unions every shown realm's items (pushTop dedupes).
* `-[all[tags]prefix[$:/GSD/Realm/]tagging[]]` — subtracts every realm-tagged item to leave the realm-less leg. Keep the subtraction form; exact-tag `!tag[$:/GSD/Realm/…]` does not mean "no realm".
* `:filter[<base>]` — constrains the union back to your base set (bare-operator start; see pitfalls below).

!! The realm warning globe

`ui/components/realm-warning` (Global, `hgsd-realm-warning(linked-tiddler)`) renders a globe beside a link whose target falls outside the ''current'' `hgsd-realm-selection` scope — the same scope the list engine filters rows with, so the globe means "this link is filtered out of your current view" and moves as you toggle the sidebar checkboxes. Consumers: the LinkItem tag list (ui/link-items/realm — rendered by hgsd-link-items after every GSD link: pick-field's set state, the prerequisites/dependants rows) and list rows themselves (a ListItem/Suffix fragment — fires on unscoped surfaces such as project pages, where outside-selection rows are still visible; on scoped dashboards outside rows are invisible by construction). One switch turns every surface off: `$:/config/hypergsd/realm-warning` (`show`/`hide`, default `show`) in Settings; 

! Pitfalls (all hit during the 2026-08-27 build — verified against core)

* Prefix-run subfilters (`:filter[…]`, `:and[…]`, `:then[…]`) must start with a ''bare'' operator run, no leading space and no leading `[`; `:filter[ [x] ]` is a parse error.
* `[title[X]]` is the safe literal form in mid-filter position; `[[X]operator[…]]` is reliable only as a filter's ''first'' run.
* A bare single-bracket run `[no-realm]` does ''not'' parse (hyphenated single-token run quirk) — always write `[[no-realm]]`; this matters inside `action-listops` subfilters, which core prefixes with `[all[]] `, placing every operand mid-filter.
* `then[<variable>]` / `else[<variable>]` do not parse — use the `:then[enlist<var>]` prefix run instead.
* Action-mode checkboxes use the `filter` attribute (non-empty output = checked) with `checkactions`/`uncheckactions` — `checked={{{…}}}` does not work.